  "title": "Hidden Price Tags Behind Your Burrito, Sneakers, iPhone, and Gas Tank",
  "summary": "Most people never think about commodities until prices go up. But from the beef in your burrito bowl to the copper in your iPhone, the rubber in your sneakers, and the gas in your car, commodity markets influence nearly every purchase you make. In this episode, Mary MacNamara sits down with Ryan Gorman, Manager of Retail Education at CME Group, to uncover how futures markets, tariffs, freight costs, supply shocks, and global events quietly shape what you pay every day.",
